# Bank check: JPMorgan Chase Bank

Observation only: this report records what the FDIC BankFind Institutions API returned for this name at the retrieval time stated below, without any API key.

Exact query: GET https://banks.data.fdic.gov/api/Institutions?filters=NAME%3AJPMorgan%2A&fields=NAME%2CCERT%2CCITY%2CSTNAME%2CACTIVE&format=json&limit=5000&sort_by=NAME&sort_order=ASC
Sent with no api_key parameter (keyless).
Retrieved (UTC): 2026-10-24T12:21:38Z
Answered from: https://api.fdic.gov/banks/Institutions?filters=NAME%3AJPMorgan%2A&fields=NAME%2CCERT%2CCITY%2CSTNAME%2CACTIVE&format=json&limit=5000&sort_by=NAME&sort_order=ASC (the API redirected the request)
FDIC index snapshot as returned: institutions_20261023090007 (createTimestamp 2026-10-23T11:54:56Z)

How the match works: the API's NAME filter is a prefix match on the whole name field, so the request below asks for every institution whose name begins with the typed name's first word; from that page, this report keeps the institutions whose name, after folding case and accents and replacing every other non letter or digit character with a space, begins with the whole typed name at a word boundary. Type the name as FDIC lists it, from its start.

The prefix page holds 3 institution(s); 2 match the typed name under the rule above.

